    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 10</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="10[a]" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ witena gerædnes is, þæt man Christene men for ealles to lytlan to deaðe ne forræde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And witena gerædnes is þæt man Christene men for ealles to lytlan to deaðe ne forræde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And the decree of the councillors is, that Christian men shall not be condemned to death for too trivial offences,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And the decree of the councilors is that Christians are not to be sentenced to death for entirely too little.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Verordnung der Witan ist, dass man christliche Menschen nicht für gar zu Geringes zum Tode verdamme.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And it is the ordinance of the witan that Christian people are not to be condemned to death for all too small [offences].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="250">[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. [?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_2-1">II Cn 2.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-009">Cn 1018 3–6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="92"><ref target="clause:IICn_2">II Cn 2–2.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><ref target="clause:IICn_2-1">II Cn 2.1</ref></note>
      </div>
